# std/stack-publish (design/stack-publish.md): an ordinary worker
# (design/tool-contract.md). It holds no token: it reads, pushes and calls the
# GitHub API through its neighbour `DEEP-DEPS/github`, the one image the
# github-token is granted to. Nothing is recorded before a push; each push's
# lease keeps it safe, and a call that does not finish is never run again
# behind the agent's back.
HELP=<<END
Publish the stack directory `root` (such as sources/repo; std/GIT.md, "Stacks") as branches and chained pull requests, in one call. The directory holds 00-base, the layers NN-<name> (gitlinks) and a description NN-<name>.pr.md beside each layer to publish: its first line is the PR title, the rest the body. Layers without a description are not published (99-dirty); a described layer above an undescribed one is refused. 00-* is never published. Each layer's branch is its name without the number, with branch-prefix in front. Repository and trunk default to 00-base.source.json. Before anything is pushed, each layer must contain the layer below it (00-base for the first): a layer that does not is refused, naming the merge to run. Then, bottom to top: push each layer as it is, find the branch's open PR or open one on the branch below (the trunk for the first), update a PR whose title or body differs from its description, and link the PRs as a GitHub stack unless link is false. Without force every push is a create or a fast-forward, leased on the branch's head as read when the call runs. With force (a rebuilt or squashed layer) pass expected, the heads you looked at: a dry run prints them in the form expected takes, and a branch that has moved since is not overwritten. The result is one line per layer (branch, commit, push outcome, PR) and the stack. A refused or failed push stops there and says what was done; run it again once that is resolved. Does not merge layers, squash, delete branches or merge PRs.
@param [branch-prefix] Text put before every branch name, such as malcolm/.
@param [repository] HTTPS repository URL, without credentials. Default: the repository 00-base was imported from.
@param [trunk] The branch the first layer's PR targets. Default: the branch 00-base was imported from, or the remote's default branch.
@param [force] true to allow non-fast-forward pushes (a rebuilt layer); needs expected.
@param [expected] With force: one line `<branch> <head>` per published layer, the head a full commit hash or `absent` for a new branch, as a dry run prints them.
@param [allow-ignored] true to publish layers whose tracked files match their .gitignore rules.
@param [link] false to leave the PRs unlinked (chained bases only). Default true: linked as a GitHub stack, so merging the top merges the stack.
@param [draft] true to open new PRs as drafts.
@param [dry-run] true to report the layers, branches, PR titles, bases and the branches' current heads, changing nothing.
@root
@request-id
END
curry --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/go --worker1:@=worker.go --github:@=DEEP-DEPS/github --help=$HELP
